<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The Medic shoulders' active, granted by the shoulders' CompProperties_AbilitiesApparel and
    fed by the injector beside it (ThingDefs_Misc/WarcasketShoulders_Medic.xml). The rules live
    in MedicWarcasket.Ability_AdrenalineShot; the walk, warmup and cast job in
    MedicWarcasket.JobDriver_AdrenalineShot (JobDefs/AdrenalineShot.xml). Design in
    Docs/Specs/Adrenaline-Shot.md.

    range is unset and requireLineOfSight off on purpose, as on the dressing: the click is not
    range-limited, the pilot walks to the patient and the job enforces distance and sight at
    distanceToTarget, 1.9: touching, diagonals included, a needle's reach. The dressing's
    autocast gives the shot at the dressing's own reach instead, where its beam just ended
    (Ability_MechaniteDressing.ShotToFollow). castTime 30 (0.5 s) is the jab, during which a
    conscious patient is held; cooldownTime 0 lets shots follow one another, the shots loaded
    being the limit. cooldownTime is a mod setting defaulting to this value; castTime and
    distanceToTarget are not.

    Targeting: an explicit targetingParametersList entry, humans and animals, no mechanoids,
    and the pilot too (canTargetSelf): a medic can inject themself, and the job skips the walk.
    Hostility and the heart are decided in ValidateTarget, not here.

    autocastPlayerDefault false: the toggle is VEF's own flag, read by the mechanite dressing's
    job rather than by VEF (which never fires an apparel ability's autocast), and offered only
    while the armor is worn. No castSound: the ability plays the injection at the patient.

    No iconPath: the mod settings write the configured reload item's uiIcon (the injector's
    ammoDef) onto def.icon at startup and on window close, so the gizmo, the cursor and the
    settings header show that item until custom ability art lands.

    The description names no reload item: the item is a mod setting, so
    Ability_AdrenalineShot appends the "Reloads with" line at runtime.
  -->
  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>
    <defName>MDWC_AdrenalineShot</defName>
    <label>adrenaline shot</label>
    <description>Inject a nearby person or animal with a dose of adrenaline drawn from a medical kit. For a few hours they feel almost no pain and move, see and think faster, while their sleep falls much faster than usual. On a patient with a heart attack the shot is spent on the heart instead.</description>
    <abilityClass>MedicWarcasket.Ability_AdrenalineShot</abilityClass>
    <gizmoClass>MedicWarcasket.Command_AdrenalineShot</gizmoClass>
    <jobDef>MDWC_AdrenalineShot</jobDef>
    <jobReportString>Giving an adrenaline shot.</jobReportString>
    <targetMode>Pawn</targetMode>
    <targetingParametersList>
      <li>
        <canTargetPawns>true</canTargetPawns>
        <canTargetHumans>true</canTargetHumans>
        <canTargetAnimals>true</canTargetAnimals>
        <canTargetMechs>false</canTargetMechs>
        <canTargetSelf>true</canTargetSelf>
        <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
        <canTargetLocations>false</canTargetLocations>
      </li>
    </targetingParametersList>
    <distanceToTarget>1.9</distanceToTarget>
    <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
    <castTime>30</castTime>
    <cooldownTime>0</cooldownTime>
    <showUndrafted>true</showUndrafted>
    <autocastPlayerDefault>false</autocastPlayerDefault>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>
</Defs>
